.TH "tum\-cheatsheet" "1" "" "" "tmux\-borrow Manual"
.SS NAME
\f[B]tum\-cheatsheet\f[R] \[em] open a popup listing every key binding
.SS SYNOPSIS
\f[B]tum cheatsheet\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]tum cheatsheet\f[R] \f[B]\-h\f[R] | \f[B]\[en]help\f[R]
.SS DESCRIPTION
Open a \f[CR]display\-popup\f[R] listing every key binding in the
shipped \f[CR]tum\-bindings.conf\f[R], grouped, so you never have to
leave tmux to remember a shortcut.
The full binding scheme is documented in \f[B]tum\-keymap\f[R](5).
.PP
Requires tmux ≥ 3.2 (\f[CR]display\-popup\f[R]).
.SS OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\[en]help\f[R] Print a short synopsis (the SYNOPSIS
and EXAMPLES sections of this page) and exit.
For bare \f[B]tum\f[R], list every subcommand.
.SS EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
tum cheatsheet           # popup of every key binding, grouped
# bound to  t ?  in the shipped tum\-bindings.conf
.EE
.SS SEE ALSO
\f[B]tum\-popup\f[R](1), \f[B]tum\-keymap\f[R](5), \f[B]tmux\f[R](1)
